  "configuration_id": "config_011",
  "reason": "Evidence: All three completed experiments share scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + multiprofile, varying only aggregation and fusion. The clear winner is config_016 (avgpool + weighted, acc=0.542, cost=2.94). The major untested dimension is the RNA encoder: we have only tried scgpt. This experiment tests scvi_n200 (a VAE-based learned representation) in place of scgpt while holding the best-performing aggregation (avgpool), fusion (weighted), image encoder (imagenet_vit_l), and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. This isolates the effect of the RNA encoder and tells us whether the current best can be improved by switching to a different learned representation. It is the best use of experiment 4 because it reduces uncertainty on the single largest unexplored architectural axis while preserving the settings that already produced the best result, and it keeps 6 experiments to exploit whichever direction wins. Expected cost: scvi_n200 is a compact VAE (200-dim latent) and should train faster than scgpt, so I estimate ~2–3 GPU hours, comparable to or slightly below config_016's 2.94."
}

